## Configuration

### Web3.Storage API Token

To configure your Web3.Storage API token:
1. Create an account on [web3.storage](https://web3.storage/)
2. Generate an API token
3. Use the "CrypTalk: Configure IPFS Storage" command to set it in the extension

### Polygon RPC URL

To configure your Polygon RPC URL:
1. Create an account with a blockchain provider like [Infura](https://infura.io/) or [Alchemy](https://www.alchemy.com/)
2. Get your Polygon Mainnet RPC URL (a default URL is already provided)
3. Use the "CrypTalk: Configure Blockchain RPC" command to set it in the extension

## Usage

### Sending Messages
1. Select a conversation or create a new one
2. Type your message in the input field
3. Click Send or press Enter

### Sending Files
1. In a conversation, click the "Upload File" button
2. Select a file from your computer
3. The file will be automatically encrypted and uploaded to IPFS
4. A link to the file will be shared in the conversation

### Cryptocurrency Payments
1. In a conversation, click the "Send Payment" button
2. Enter the recipient's address (or use the conversation partner's address)
3. Enter the amount to send
4. Confirm the transaction

### Creating Group Chats
1. Click "New Chat" and select "Group Chat"
2. Enter a name for the group
3. Add participants by entering their wallet addresses or inbox IDs
4. Click "Create"

## Privacy and Security

- All messages are end-to-end encrypted
- Files are encrypted before being uploaded to IPFS
- Your private keys never leave your browser
- No central server stores your conversation history
- Decentralized architecture ensures no single point of failure

## Technical Details

This extension is built using:
- Cryptalk SDK (based on XMTP protocol)
- IPFS/Web3.Storage for decentralized file storage
- Ethers.js for blockchain interactions
- CryptoJS for encryption/decryption
- React for the user interface

